---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
import ProjectTags from "../../components/ProjectTags.astro";
import RoverArchitecture from "../../components/RoverArchitecture.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout>
  {/* HERO */}
  <section id="overview" class="mb-12">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Autonomous Rover</h1>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700 max-w-3xl">
          <li>Camera-guided rover for disk collection, ramp traversal, and delivery.</li>
          <li>My work: perception, behavior sequencing, and encoder-based wheel control.</li>
        </ul>

        <ProjectTags />
      </div>

      {/* HERO MEDIA */}
      <div class="rounded-lg shadow-md overflow-hidden w-full">
        <video
          class="w-full h-auto"
          autoplay
          controls
          muted
          loop
          playsinline
          preload="metadata"
          poster="/media/autonomous-rover/hero-poster.png"
        >
          <source src="/media/autonomous-rover/hero.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          {/* Fallback for ancient browsers */}
          <img
            src="/media/autonomous-rover/final-assembly.jpg"
            alt="Autonomous rover prototype transporting disks"
            class="w-full h-auto"
          />
        </video>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* PROBLEM + CONSTRAINTS */}
  <section id="course" class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Problem & Constraints</h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start">
      <div class="text-gray-700 space-y-3">
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
          <li>Follow the line through curves, intersections, and a 15° ramp.</li>
          <li>Collect and deliver at least two disks in the specified order; bonus for three.</li>
          <li>Meet size limits and remain functional after a short drop test.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <img
        src="/media/autonomous-rover/venue-diagram.png"
        alt="Testing venue diagram showing start, pickup, ramp, and drop-off zones"
        class="rounded-lg shadow-sm w-full"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* SYSTEM OVERVIEW 2 */}
  <section id="hardware" class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">System Overview</h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start">
      <div class="text-gray-700 space-y-4">

        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3 text-gray-600">
          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">Raspberry Pi:</span>
            ROS 2 perception, behavior logic, and velocity commands.
          </li>

          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">Arduino Nano:</span>
            Independent encoder-based wheel-speed control; PD gains with Ki = 0.
          </li>

          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">L298N driver:</span>
            Two 12 V DC motors with encoders.
          </li>

          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">Power:</span>
            12 V battery and buck converter supply the motors, logic, and servos.
          </li>

          <li>
            <span class="font-medium">Development laptop:</span>
            SSH access, logging, and ROS image inspection.
          </li>
        </ul>

      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <img
          src="/media/autonomous-rover/ros-network-architecture.png"
          alt="ROS 2 communication architecture between robot_ws and dev_ws"
          class="rounded-lg shadow-sm w-full"
        />

        <img
          src="/media/autonomous-rover/electronics-schematic.png"
          alt="Electronics and wiring layout of rover components"
          class="rounded-lg shadow-sm w-full"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* MECHANICAL */}
  <section id="mechanical-design" class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Mechanical Design</h2>

    {/* KEY SPECS */}
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-8">
      <div class="rounded-lg border bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Dimensions (L×W×H)</div>
        <div class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">29.9 × 24.1 × 16.4 cm</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Total mass</div>
        <div class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">2.902 kg</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Max ramp</div>
        <div class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">15° with 3 disks</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border bg-white p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="text-sm text-gray-500">Speed targets</div>
        <div class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">5–15 cm/s</div>
        <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">~10 cm/s straight, ~8 cm/s turns</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      <div class="rounded-lg border bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">Chassis</h3>
        <img class="rounded-md mb-3" src="/media/autonomous-rover/cad-overview.png" alt="Assembled rover CAD overview" />
        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
          Layered chassis with access to electronics and drive components.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">Basket Lift</h3>
        <img class="rounded-md mb-3" src="/media/autonomous-rover/basket-lift.png" alt="Basket lift crank-slider mechanism" />
        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
          Crank-slider mechanism raises the basket to the drop-off platform.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-2">Scoop Arm</h3>
        <img class="rounded-md mb-3" src="/media/autonomous-rover/arm-rack-pinion.png" alt="Rack and pinion scoop arm mechanism" />
        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
          Servo-driven rack-and-pinion extension for disk pickup and unloading.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

  </section>

  {/* CONTROLS */}
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Controls & Autonomy</h2>

    <div class="text-gray-700 space-y-10">

      {/* HIGH-LEVEL STACK */}
      <div>
        <p class="text-gray-600">
          The autonomy stack was structured as:
          <span class="font-medium">perception → behavior → motion mapping → closed-loop control → actuation</span>.
          ROS 2 handled inter-node communication and behavior sequencing,
          while the Arduino maintained deterministic wheel velocity control.
        </p>
      </div>

      {/* ROS ARCHITECTURE */}
      <div id="ros-architecture" class="space-y-3">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">ROS 2 Architecture</h3>
        <RoverArchitecture />
      </div>

      {/* PERCEPTION */}
      <div id="perception" class="space-y-3">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Computer Vision Pipeline</h3>

        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
          <li>ROS image → OpenCV via <code>cv_bridge</code></li>
          <li>Bird's-eye mapping, grayscale and thresholding to isolate the black track</li>
          <li>Morphological cleanup → contour detection → select largest contour</li>
          <li>Line estimate → publish a lateral position as <code>/line_position</code></li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-gray-600">
          The vision pipeline estimates the line's lateral position relative to
          the image center and uses that error for steering.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4">Special Case Handling</h4>

        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
          <li><span class="font-mono">x ≥ 0</span> → normal tracking</li>
          <li><span class="font-mono">x = -3 / -4</span> → sharp turn detected (bounding box hits an edge)</li>
          <li><span class="font-mono">x = -2</span> → intersection detected (box hits both edges) → behavior handoff</li>
          <li><span class="font-mono">x = -1</span> → line lost → slow reverse / recovery search</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      {/* CV steering diagram */}
      <figure id="perception-output" class="mt-5 rounded-lg border bg-white shadow-sm overflow-hidden">
        <img
          src="/media/autonomous-rover/cv-steering-diagram.jpg"
          alt="Computer vision steering: segmented regions and extracted line center used to compute lateral error"
          class="w-full h-auto block"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="px-4 py-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
          CV steering output: the pipeline isolates the line, extracts its x-center, and produces a lateral error signal used for steering.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      {/* DIFFERENTIAL DRIVE */}
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Differential Drive Mapping</h3>

        <p class="text-gray-600">
          ROS velocity commands use <code>linear.x</code> (forward) and
          <code>angular.z</code> (turn). These were mapped to wheel velocities using:
        </p>

        <pre class="rounded-md bg-gray-50 border p-4 text-sm overflow-auto">
  v_left  = v - ω · L / 2
  v_right = v + ω · L / 2
  wheel_rate_left  = v_left / r
  wheel_rate_right = v_right / r
        </pre>

        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">
          Here v is forward speed in m/s, ω is counterclockwise yaw rate in rad/s,
          L is wheel separation in meters, and r is wheel radius in meters.
          Wheel rates are rad/s, using a no-slip kinematic model.
        </p>
      </div>

      {/* CLOSED LOOP CONTROL */}
      <div id="wheel-control" class="space-y-3">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg">Closed-Loop Wheel Control</h3>

        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
          <li>Encoder resolution: ~1975 counts per revolution</li>
          <li>Control loop frequency: 30 Hz</li>
          <li>Baseline command: PWM ≈ 70 (0–255) → ~1 rev/s</li>
          <li>PID implementation with PD gains: Kp = 20, Kd = 12, Ki = 0, Ko = 50 (implementation-specific scaling)</li>
        </ul>

        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
          <li>Tuned proportional and derivative gains using wheel-speed step-response tests, with Ki = 0.</li>
          <li>Tested the gains under varying loads and battery conditions.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>


    </div>
  </section>

  {/* RESULTS*/}
  <section id="results" class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Results & Performance</h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
      <div class="text-gray-700 space-y-4">

        <h3 class="font-semibold">System Performance</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
          <li>Full course: <span class="font-medium">&lt; 5 minutes</span> with smooth camera input. Completion was inconsistent; success rate was not measured.</li>
          <li>Ramp traversal + curved segment: <span class="font-medium">28–32 seconds</span>.</li>
          <li>Per disk: pickup <span class="font-medium">3–4 seconds</span>; unload <span class="font-medium">5–6 seconds</span>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-semibold mt-6">Observed Challenges</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
          <li>Camera startup failures and image lag caused late corrections and overshoot.</li>
          <li>Reduced image resolution and added adaptive velocity scaling to mitigate delay.</li>
          <li>Full-system tests exposed timing and coordination issues missed by module tests.</li>
        </ul>

      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <figure class="rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden bg-white border">
          <video
            class="w-full h-auto"
            autoplay
            controls
            muted
            loop
            playsinline
            preload="metadata"
          >
            <source src="/media/autonomous-rover/demo-pickup.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
          <figcaption class="px-3 py-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
            Disk pickup sequence (3–4 s cycle)
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure class="rounded-lg shadow-sm overflow-hidden bg-white border">
          <video
            class="w-full h-auto"
            autoplay
            controls
            muted
            loop
            playsinline
            preload="metadata"
          >
            <source src="/media/autonomous-rover/demo-dropoff.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
          <figcaption class="px-3 py-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
            Drop-off sequence (5–6 s unload cycle)
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* LESSONS*/}
  <section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Lessons Learned & Next Steps</h2>

    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3 text-gray-600">

      <li>Begin integrated perception and motion tests earlier.</li>
      <li>Measure observation age from image capture to command receipt.</li>
      <li>Compare camera and infrared line sensing under repeatable course conditions.</li>

    </ul>
  </section>

</ProjectLayout>

<style>
  [id] { scroll-margin-top: 7rem; }
</style>
